sentences.t:
Hic, quos durus amor crudeli tabe peredit,
secreti celant calles et myrtea circum
silva tegit;

sentences.l:
Here those whom hard love with cruel wasting has eaten away,
secluded hide paths, and a myrtle round about
wood covers;

sentences.t:
His Phaedram Procrimque locis, maestamque Eriphylen
crudelis nati monstrantem volnera, cernit,
Evadnenque et Pasiphaën;

sentences.l:
In these Phaedra and Procris places, and sorrowful Eriphyle,
of her cruel son showing the wounds, he sees,
and Evadne and Pasiphaë;

sentences.t:
At Danaum proceres Agamemnoniaeque phalanges
ut videre virum fulgentiaque arma per umbras,
ingenti trepidare metu;

sentences.l:
But of the Danaans the chiefs and Agamemnon's phalanxes,
when they saw the man and his gleaming arms through the shadows,
with huge to tremble fear;
